pokeheartgold-tags.patch (tools/pokehg_gen.py applies the patches in name order): Smooth motion's tags, the pseudo-command
that names the game object each 3D list belongs to (libntr's simulator/sim_g3tag.h), so the in-betweens can pair sprites,
shadows, effects and particles by identity. Sites: the billboard list draw sub_02023950 (a field sprite, the follower
Pokemon's too: its list, the billboard, the texture and palette indexes its animation shows), the anim managers' render loop
sub_02068BAC (a field effect, the water ring and the grass rustle among them: its render function, the anim manager), the two
shadow render functions ov01_021FD7D4 and ov01_021FD980 (the 6-vertex lists drawn before the sprites; inst = the map
object's sprite's, the anchor), lib/spl's two particle draw loops (the emitter, the particle, its age); each loop ends with
the empty tag. The places that make a billboard (sub_02024280), an anim manager (sub_02068A08), an emitter or a particle
again drop its old id (SIM_G3TagDrop). Off (the default) each site is one flag test and the command stream is unchanged;
BWPORT_VCAPTURE_TAGS=1 or SIM_G3TagEnable(1) turns them on. Platinum's twin is pokeplatinum-tags.patch.
Handover-ID: none (port-only)

